  "Food board and tray:": "食品板和托盤：",
  "Food board and tray: Eight large food tiles are available. Tap the pictured foods to build a tray, then tap the matching customer. Clear the tray before delivery if the selection is wrong.": "食物板和托盤：有八個大食物塊可供選擇。點擊圖中的食物來建立一個托盤，然後點擊匹配的顧客。如果選擇錯誤，請在出貨前清除托盤。",
  "Food card drag area": "餐卡拖曳區",
  "Food Clue": "食物線索",
  "Food effects": "食物影響",
  "Food to sort": "待分類的食物",
  "Foods alternate between warm and cool groups.": "食物在暖性和涼性之間交替。",
  "Foque um alvo por vez.": "Foque um alvo por vez。",
  "For a big-match goal, build around four or five aligned snacks instead of relying on a random refill.": "對於大型比賽的目標，圍繞四到五種對齊的零食進行準備，而不是依賴隨機補充。",
  "For a moving basket, aim for where it will be after the bounce rather than where it was at Cut.": "對於移動的籃子，瞄準彈跳後的位置，而不是切入時的位置。",
  "For a moving basket, watch its direction and aim at the position it will occupy when the fruit comes down, not its position at Cut.": "對於移動的籃子，觀察它的方向並瞄準水果落下時它所佔據的位置，而不是它在切割時的位置。",
  "For a remembered request, tap the animal and look again instead of guessing.": "對於記住的請求，請點擊動物並再次查看而不是猜測。",
  "For cascade goals, leave a nearly complete match above the row you plan to clear.": "對於級聯目標，在您計劃清除的行上方留下幾乎完整的匹配。",
  "For category play, decide whether each picture means food, drink, cleaning or play.": "對於類別遊戲，確定每張圖片是否代表食物、飲料、清潔或遊戲。",
  "For families": "對於家庭",
  "For fun and local progress tracking only.": "僅用於娛樂和本地進度追蹤。",
  "For memory play, name the hidden symbol aloud or trace its outline in the air.": "對於記憶遊戲，大聲說出隱藏符號的名稱或在空中描繪其輪廓。",
  "For memory play, name the symbol aloud or trace its outline in the air.": "對於記憶遊戲，請大聲說出符號的名稱或在空中描繪其輪廓。",
  "For sealed missions, plan three legs in advance: treasure seal, mission object, and extraction. Missions 29 and 30 relocate the last leg, so preserve Alert capacity for the new exit.": "封印任務，事先規劃好三條腿：寶藏封印、任務目標、撤離。任務 29 和 30 重新定位最後一段，因此保留新出口的警報容量。",
  "For silhouettes, compare outline clues such as a trunk, long neck, shell, ears, or body shape.": "對於剪影，比較輪廓線索，例如軀幹、長脖子、貝殼、耳朵或身體形狀。",
  "For silhouettes, compare the outline of trunks, necks, shells, ears and bodies.": "對於輪廓，比較軀幹、頸部、貝殼、耳朵和身體的輪廓。",
  "For stairs, emphasize vertical height; for a tunnel, lower the top while keeping enough width.": "對於樓梯，強調垂直高度；對於隧道，降低頂部，同時保持足夠的寬度。",
  "For variety, remember the last animal served and look for another eligible species.": "對於多樣性，請記住最後提供的動物並尋找其他符合條件的物種。",
  "For variety, remember the last animal served and look for another species.": "為了多樣化，請記住最後供應的動物並尋找其他物種。",
